      "title": "Jaw die wear zones",
      "description": "The dies wear fastest in the lower third, near the closed-side setting, where the gap is tightest and most of the crushing work is done (purple). Wear there opens the setting and makes the product coarser, so the setting is re-adjusted with shims or wedges. Many dies are symmetrical and can be turned top-to-bottom once to use the less-worn upper part.",
